[{:db/id "q-336603/field-1/6f1b1e6d6efb3e49f546f382ebd2796d1934aeda46cab4a4fd746b3290da22d0" :answer/id #uuid "5082b3e5-a1d3-517a-a68c-73f10278ced3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336603/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "88ab049f-725b-5c2b-b12d-88d29591265c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336603/field-1/6f1b1e6d6efb3e49f546f382ebd2796d1934aeda46cab4a4fd746b3290da22d0" :answer-field/choices ["q-336603/field-1/6f1b1e6d6efb3e49f546f382ebd2796d1934aeda46cab4a4fd746b3290da22d0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336603" :question/id #uuid "c8d8efae-b2c7-55a2-a0c7-7d7b3a2c7eb2" :question/math-academy-id "q-336603" :question/problem "Compute the exact value of the definite integral.\n\n${\\int }_{-7/10}^{-1/5}\\sqrt{10x+7}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We start by changing the variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =10x+7 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =10 \\\\ \\text{d}u & =10\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{10}\\text{d}u & =\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we create a table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=10x+7.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & -\\frac{7}{10} & -\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ u & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-7/10}^{-1/5}\\sqrt{10x+7}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{5}\\sqrt{u}\\,\\cdot \\frac{1}{10}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve it and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{5}\\sqrt{u}\\,\\cdot \\frac{1}{10}\\,\\text{d}u & =\\frac{1}{10}{\\int }_{0}^{5}{u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\cdot {\\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2}|}_{0}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}({5}^{3/2}-{0}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{15}(({5}^{3})^{1/2}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{15}\\cdot 5\\sqrt{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-336603/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9dcde3b5-5cdf-5266-9392-0835053a7ded"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336603"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-318994/field-1/b239fdfe9a18cef34e07732b84b6404ab25cd9ff1faf8d4ebd55fc595a0309bf" :answer/id #uuid "58dec1c3-275e-5d97-80f2-e7c287f3e297" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{671}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-318994/field-1/36dfc86af2f633faf83435b8bac73c2a4a0f92640be5fb4d513d55450efe5630" :answer/id #uuid "cddeeabc-dea8-53a9-b433-f9ae386435c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "671" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-318994/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d939e60f-7845-57c4-91ae-d7e8f543554c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-318994/field-1/b239fdfe9a18cef34e07732b84b6404ab25cd9ff1faf8d4ebd55fc595a0309bf" :answer-field/choices ["q-318994/field-1/b239fdfe9a18cef34e07732b84b6404ab25cd9ff1faf8d4ebd55fc595a0309bf" "q-318994/field-1/36dfc86af2f633faf83435b8bac73c2a4a0f92640be5fb4d513d55450efe5630"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-318994" :question/id #uuid "0734ee69-ce40-5cea-a446-6590c63b381e" :question/math-academy-id "q-318994" :question/problem "Compute the exact value of the definite integral.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}6{x}^{2}\\cdot {({x}^{3}+5)}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We start by changing the variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & ={x}^{3}+5 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2} \\\\ \\text{d}u & =3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 6{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\,\\text{d}u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we create a table for the limits of integration using the rule $u={x}^{3}+5.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & 0 & 1 \\\\ u & 5 & 6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}6{x}^{2}\\cdot {({x}^{3}+5)}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{5}^{6}{u}^{3}\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve it and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{5}^{6}2{u}^{3}\\,\\text{d}u & =2{\\int }_{5}^{6}{u}^{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\cdot {\\frac{{u}^{4}}{4}|}_{5}^{6} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}({6}^{4}-{5}^{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1296-625) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 671 \\\\  & =\\frac{671}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-318994/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9dcde3b5-5cdf-5266-9392-0835053a7ded"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-318994"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-17103/selection/996a704392b82380114fb75b164d978cb636f2a028e1fae21abf1827814dd363" :answer/id #uuid "286525e4-60f9-541e-a0c4-46995ac66a7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{484}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17103/selection/1824d1277b9e650db9bd2ecf012f302012ca31e739170457eea3c0759d91a02c" :answer/id #uuid "26c816eb-4186-5d17-8d26-9bf774a9a4a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{844}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17103/selection/50243d316b735d61d679270c33ea77f72d6a9ef86b866ca12822bc02b079c957" :answer/id #uuid "1a8e270b-fe9f-59d1-a7df-5c52bcbaa246" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{48}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17103/selection/46a53d47d0b009b31713778abe2d1f40f22bc7aaea4b508b1040ecf3a95825f3" :answer/id #uuid "26dfb02b-952e-51af-9728-d45ce9eb7d38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{448}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17103/selection/4032824ca6b060adf2da25de6ac333f84588f3c31f8ef1a0b548e27211c1f6a1" :answer/id #uuid "05a8004e-bdbd-5828-aa03-6e55f2f0c732" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{844}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17103/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8899b9d4-ec60-5237-b82a-86d8cabd9e00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-17103/selection/996a704392b82380114fb75b164d978cb636f2a028e1fae21abf1827814dd363" :answer-field/choices ["q-17103/selection/996a704392b82380114fb75b164d978cb636f2a028e1fae21abf1827814dd363" "q-17103/selection/1824d1277b9e650db9bd2ecf012f302012ca31e739170457eea3c0759d91a02c" "q-17103/selection/50243d316b735d61d679270c33ea77f72d6a9ef86b866ca12822bc02b079c957" "q-17103/selection/46a53d47d0b009b31713778abe2d1f40f22bc7aaea4b508b1040ecf3a95825f3" "q-17103/selection/4032824ca6b060adf2da25de6ac333f84588f3c31f8ef1a0b548e27211c1f6a1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-17103" :question/id #uuid "63c0bfbc-06ab-5f65-8f01-cf35b1de1276" :question/math-academy-id "q-17103" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{2}3{x}^{2}\\sqrt{{({x}^{3}+1)}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We start by changing the variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & ={x}^{3}+1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2} \\\\ \\text{d}u & =3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we create a table for the limits of integration using the rule $u={x}^{3}+1.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & 0 & 2 \\\\ u & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{{({x}^{3}+1)}^{3}}\\cdot 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{1}^{9}\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve it and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{9}\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}u & ={\\int }_{1}^{9}{u}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\frac{2}{5}{u}^{5/2}|}_{1}^{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}({9}^{5/2}-{1}^{5/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}(({3}^{2})^{5/2}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}({3}^{5}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{484}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-17103/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9dcde3b5-5cdf-5266-9392-0835053a7ded"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-17103"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-336612/field-1/5521c093c4d60c23d630a99bc791ac7318f4615e164361df756510ffc0408a97" :answer/id #uuid "9d20ab54-95ec-580b-b4d7-a1308803f9a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{14}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336612/field-1/cedce138738816f1e959edfd5049bf0c6bcf0acc69b898c7f84479cb3a782ce3" :answer/id #uuid "09333cda-07b2-5e5f-8923-acd8083e9f69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336612/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "3af30cd5-8c6d-5b3a-a13e-d5d1931697f8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336612/field-1/5521c093c4d60c23d630a99bc791ac7318f4615e164361df756510ffc0408a97" :answer-field/choices ["q-336612/field-1/5521c093c4d60c23d630a99bc791ac7318f4615e164361df756510ffc0408a97" "q-336612/field-1/cedce138738816f1e959edfd5049bf0c6bcf0acc69b898c7f84479cb3a782ce3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336612" :question/id #uuid "ea5b8eb2-9335-5efb-9a82-40d5dd89b435" :question/math-academy-id "q-336612" :question/problem "Compute the exact value of the definite integral.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}8{x}^{3}\\cdot {({x}^{4}+1)}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We start by changing the variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & ={x}^{4}+1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =4{x}^{3} \\\\ \\text{d}u & =4{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 8{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\,\\text{d}u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we create a table for the limits of integration using the rule $u={x}^{4}+1.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & 0 & 1 \\\\ u & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}8{x}^{3}\\cdot {({x}^{4}+1)}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{1}^{2}{u}^{2}\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve it and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}2{u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u & =2{\\int }_{1}^{2}{u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\cdot {\\frac{{u}^{3}}{3}|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}({2}^{3}-{1}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(8-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-336612/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9dcde3b5-5cdf-5266-9392-0835053a7ded"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336612"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-336803/field-1/8dcc5cebca424352e64e1c36b646a73a4f3f64cd04cbf5e5c37ee2f167875a6f" :answer/id #uuid "1a38641c-d3cb-5b45-b7d9-4ab708b3ea41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{62}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336803/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "db06b4af-0dfe-5b1d-9c31-39b5385a2cde" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336803/field-1/8dcc5cebca424352e64e1c36b646a73a4f3f64cd04cbf5e5c37ee2f167875a6f" :answer-field/choices ["q-336803/field-1/8dcc5cebca424352e64e1c36b646a73a4f3f64cd04cbf5e5c37ee2f167875a6f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336803" :question/id #uuid "7e407f67-4ad5-59db-a798-bfbd7a1050f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-336803" :question/problem "Compute the exact value of the definite integral.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}2x\\sqrt{{({x}^{2}+1)}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We start by changing the variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & ={x}^{2}+1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =2x \\\\ \\text{d}u & =2x\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we create a table for the limits of integration using the rule $u={x}^{2}+1.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & 0 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ u & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\sqrt{{({x}^{2}+1)}^{3}}\\cdot 2x\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve it and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}u & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}{u}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\frac{2}{5}{u}^{5/2}|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}({4}^{5/2}-{1}^{5/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}(({2}^{2})^{5/2}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}({2}^{5}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{62}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-336803/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9dcde3b5-5cdf-5266-9392-0835053a7ded"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336803"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-13189/selection/2d071a6e1d5d555e04a72a0e6dd6f66de3e8dcc617676d80ae8f449b7dc4792c" :answer/id #uuid "958ab2a8-29b1-5452-b6e6-6ead26cba627" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-13189/selection/624f749b4f86cfa17747f88c1651a75abc86d25b53c10d6090ee357071d56b29" :answer/id #uuid "d5f7897e-fcb8-51da-9eeb-54fc0edcfb21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-13189/selection/7a152297408acc143c00745c3ed3cdfe54cde6305dd3cb03267526c5d92b80f9" :answer/id #uuid "e5ada9ec-283c-5993-b575-735c9320a3ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-13189/selection/1afec9675aad10820fc48fc9d480c6cd2c37b443053a148155069e5df3205082" :answer/id #uuid "141ef4a6-0c75-5da0-9e5c-44c97286349b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-13189/selection/9150572d7444bfdae5c2db83fd4384f4365a80e8daa3e6090fefdc804d1901eb" :answer/id #uuid "4dd8f7ea-d149-5201-8f52-ab0239496509" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-13189/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3e3cc8a2-ab0b-5baf-a7ad-355d3f8cfeb7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-13189/selection/1afec9675aad10820fc48fc9d480c6cd2c37b443053a148155069e5df3205082" :answer-field/choices ["q-13189/selection/2d071a6e1d5d555e04a72a0e6dd6f66de3e8dcc617676d80ae8f449b7dc4792c" "q-13189/selection/624f749b4f86cfa17747f88c1651a75abc86d25b53c10d6090ee357071d56b29" "q-13189/selection/7a152297408acc143c00745c3ed3cdfe54cde6305dd3cb03267526c5d92b80f9" "q-13189/selection/1afec9675aad10820fc48fc9d480c6cd2c37b443053a148155069e5df3205082" "q-13189/selection/9150572d7444bfdae5c2db83fd4384f4365a80e8daa3e6090fefdc804d1901eb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-13189" :question/id #uuid "10b22c83-a900-5845-9fa8-2b1a58314a4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-13189" :question/problem "Evaluate the definite integral ${\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{3x+2}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We start by changing the variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =3x+2 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =3 \\\\ \\text{d}u & =3\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u & =\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we create a table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=3x+2.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & 1 & 2 \\\\ u & 5 & 8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{(3x+2)}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{5}^{8}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve it and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{5}^{8}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{5}^{8}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(u){|}_{5}^{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({2}^{3})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-13189/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d63e99a-9db4-565e-97c5-ffc3090b0074"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-13189"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-19129/selection/f02455f22a06a055a0dcf1feada84e4b7e05ccb62d3798940c3094ff0b0130c5" :answer/id #uuid "557a4692-d847-5d73-98b6-0bf90fc3be98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19129/selection/b3500c059be2582acdf66490b5d907744abbf130df1a688ff5bc4c95f6039c63" :answer/id #uuid "4b364dd6-024d-5a32-9676-a166e385e767" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19129/selection/9873627a71630bf040908291ba4613d755a1f46f62469c2b6310ea8c916119b7" :answer/id #uuid "50ec821d-517f-53a6-b572-fb601139d44c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19129/selection/286a23b4f88ab5c5f58674d94dd3996a24158cd522f456ca4f7fa96ef4dc831e" :answer/id #uuid "7ab74861-12dd-56ab-af85-2e388e33b0dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19129/selection/7666171b9fd856fb97e1f99d874bc0a0d50c0ee4241ecdf375368703b1cc498c" :answer/id #uuid "f831ed64-076e-5599-b7ce-787261bcd6d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19129/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7976a714-1030-5277-99d0-b6864958a0f9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-19129/selection/b3500c059be2582acdf66490b5d907744abbf130df1a688ff5bc4c95f6039c63" :answer-field/choices ["q-19129/selection/f02455f22a06a055a0dcf1feada84e4b7e05ccb62d3798940c3094ff0b0130c5" "q-19129/selection/b3500c059be2582acdf66490b5d907744abbf130df1a688ff5bc4c95f6039c63" "q-19129/selection/9873627a71630bf040908291ba4613d755a1f46f62469c2b6310ea8c916119b7" "q-19129/selection/286a23b4f88ab5c5f58674d94dd3996a24158cd522f456ca4f7fa96ef4dc831e" "q-19129/selection/7666171b9fd856fb97e1f99d874bc0a0d50c0ee4241ecdf375368703b1cc498c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-19129" :question/id #uuid "f8f07d6e-aebe-5b7e-9e51-0e3439a6a7cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-19129" :question/problem "Calculate the definite integral ${\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{4x}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We start by changing the variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =1+{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =2x \\\\ \\text{d}u & =2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 2\\,\\text{d}u & =4x\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we create a table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=1+{x}^{2}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & 0 & 2 \\\\ u & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{(1+{x}^{2})}\\cdot 4x\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{1}^{5}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve it and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{5}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}u & =2{\\int }_{1}^{5}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(u){|}_{1}^{5} \\\\  & =2(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-19129/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d63e99a-9db4-565e-97c5-ffc3090b0074"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-19129"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73432/selection/2c03b26f4279877c28980a7281f56a8186af49847b7c9fdb72803b2a41bb88dc" :answer/id #uuid "de6eac51-5ed0-5ae3-ad45-4c8e808a1e68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73432/selection/a28cc998fd82186c1f416633d22d66af3de7291093873728bc237e66c06e680f" :answer/id #uuid "7d956354-a411-5f73-9663-586be922e240" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{5}{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73432/selection/9c8bed75f44951ce2edfeb9367cb66172ead6877ece2918f8765cf62220c5580" :answer/id #uuid "4aa26fc9-f7c0-536a-85e7-fb53721fb180" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73432/selection/5b32059b32fb58b154c7bdac15a89eb615150532f2063bad0ba33ca1e05d8d73" :answer/id #uuid "faf62a37-808a-5111-a65a-fbc2c71853dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73432/selection/1a83b363f077101c679b7f65d52038347988664a430c033a40e2fa2f790767ab" :answer/id #uuid "09e1f14f-36a3-5fb5-af37-568e066845ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{5}{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73432/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2d7d72e0-4d11-52ca-80cb-919ecfd57e61" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73432/selection/1a83b363f077101c679b7f65d52038347988664a430c033a40e2fa2f790767ab" :answer-field/choices ["q-73432/selection/2c03b26f4279877c28980a7281f56a8186af49847b7c9fdb72803b2a41bb88dc" "q-73432/selection/a28cc998fd82186c1f416633d22d66af3de7291093873728bc237e66c06e680f" "q-73432/selection/9c8bed75f44951ce2edfeb9367cb66172ead6877ece2918f8765cf62220c5580" "q-73432/selection/5b32059b32fb58b154c7bdac15a89eb615150532f2063bad0ba33ca1e05d8d73" "q-73432/selection/1a83b363f077101c679b7f65d52038347988664a430c033a40e2fa2f790767ab"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73432" :question/id #uuid "ba2d9110-9750-574a-89bb-6445eeb6564f" :question/math-academy-id "q-73432" :question/problem "Calculate the definite integral ${\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{x}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We start by changing the variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & ={x}^{4}+9 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =4{x}^{3} \\\\ \\text{d}u & =4{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u & ={x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we create a table for the limits of integration using the rule $u={x}^{4}+9.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & 0 & 2 \\\\ u & 9 & 25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{({x}^{4}+9)}\\,{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{9}^{25}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve it and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{9}^{25}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{9}^{25}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(u){|}_{9}^{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(25)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({5}^{2})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({3}^{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 2(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{5}{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-73432/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d63e99a-9db4-565e-97c5-ffc3090b0074"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73432"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-336729/field-1/a0d0bc96d7f89f9928f267c3f4944055628442fbc9faa554cbf6c6e7f1c15f49" :answer/id #uuid "35d5bc15-85bf-5bdf-bbe4-f38a99251259" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\ln(3)-\\ln(2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336729/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ecc3563d-3cb0-5d60-9aa4-b0f056c44486" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336729/field-1/a0d0bc96d7f89f9928f267c3f4944055628442fbc9faa554cbf6c6e7f1c15f49" :answer-field/choices ["q-336729/field-1/a0d0bc96d7f89f9928f267c3f4944055628442fbc9faa554cbf6c6e7f1c15f49"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336729" :question/id #uuid "db508ded-c280-5a2c-90e1-2eecaec60c11" :question/math-academy-id "q-336729" :question/problem "Compute the exact value of the definite integral.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{10{x}^{3}}{5{x}^{4}+4}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We start by changing the variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =5{x}^{4}+4 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =20{x}^{3} \\\\ \\text{d}u & =20{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{20}\\text{d}u & ={x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we create a table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=5{x}^{4}+4.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & 0 & 1 \\\\ u & 4 & 9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{10{x}^{3}}{(5{x}^{4}+4)}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{4}^{9}\\frac{10}{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{20}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve it and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4}^{9}\\frac{10}{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{20}\\text{d}u & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{4}^{9}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(u){|}_{4}^{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{9}{4}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-336729/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d63e99a-9db4-565e-97c5-ffc3090b0074"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336729"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73434/selection/19d3f489ba69612714d09da9c09f7acb98141a3dcf92231976208e758f1bc376" :answer/id #uuid "028aaa85-487e-5894-95b5-3c6f9f8cc266" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73434/selection/45e529772872b55eb572b8dbc78378901c61ad3eb614d193f1f8aacc38d68391" :answer/id #uuid "68066a7a-861d-5b34-b347-cbd023a93ae4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73434/selection/5a62d209c00aa152c6e1fd8ec3e1ca2b0540c6d7cf3a7c4baae55dbbc5eb7d41" :answer/id #uuid "c07b38ef-860b-5227-ad74-4babb273e31e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73434/selection/e0588ee0ca6541459cfbad0e2eb8905ffdd044185ae0828f8af61da59ff909cf" :answer/id #uuid "593b5515-f3bb-560e-94cc-272bebd5aae2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73434/selection/21fdd4e4f76fc36548aec007920d17a0395b52c13891c3718a699d850503eaf4" :answer/id #uuid "57487ef3-c506-5ed3-8555-102072511111" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73434/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "86b8cb96-c9cb-5598-8329-d953b01627a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73434/selection/5a62d209c00aa152c6e1fd8ec3e1ca2b0540c6d7cf3a7c4baae55dbbc5eb7d41" :answer-field/choices ["q-73434/selection/19d3f489ba69612714d09da9c09f7acb98141a3dcf92231976208e758f1bc376" "q-73434/selection/45e529772872b55eb572b8dbc78378901c61ad3eb614d193f1f8aacc38d68391" "q-73434/selection/5a62d209c00aa152c6e1fd8ec3e1ca2b0540c6d7cf3a7c4baae55dbbc5eb7d41" "q-73434/selection/e0588ee0ca6541459cfbad0e2eb8905ffdd044185ae0828f8af61da59ff909cf" "q-73434/selection/21fdd4e4f76fc36548aec007920d17a0395b52c13891c3718a699d850503eaf4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73434" :question/id #uuid "f292e871-dc0d-583a-95a2-02c1d9aad59f" :question/math-academy-id "q-73434" :question/problem "Calculate the definite integral ${\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{3}+2}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We start by changing the variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & ={x}^{3}+2 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2} \\\\ \\text{d}u & =3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u & ={x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we create a table for the limits of integration using the rule $u={x}^{3}+2.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & -1 & 1 \\\\ u & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{1}{({x}^{3}+2)}\\,{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve it and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(u){|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-73434/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d63e99a-9db4-565e-97c5-ffc3090b0074"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73434"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-455"] :question/problem "Calculate the definite integral $\\displaystyle\\int_{-1}^0 x(x^2+1)^3\\,\\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We start by changing the variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & ={x}^{2}+1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =2x \\\\ \\text{d}u & =2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u & =x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we create a table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=x^2+1.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & -1 & 0 \\\\ u & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n\\int_{-1}^0 x(x^2+1)^3\\,\\textrm{d}x=\\int_2^1 u^3\\,\\cdot \\dfrac{1}{2}\\textrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve it and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{1}{u}^{3}\\,\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{2}^{1}{u}^{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{4}}{4}{|}_{2}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{{1}^{4}-{2}^{4}}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1-16}{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{15}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Important**: Note that in this example, when we changed the limits the integral $\\displaystyle \\int_{-1}^0 \\ldots \\textrm{d}x$ became $\\displaystyle \\int_{2}^1 \\ldots \\textrm{d}u.$ When changing the limits, it is important to respect the order in which the limits are applied. The lower limit of the integral in $u$ must correspond to the lower limit of the integral in $x.$ Same for the upper limit." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-456"] :question/problem "Calculate the definite integral $\\displaystyle\\int_{-1}^2 \\dfrac{x^2}{x^3+2}\\,\\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We start by changing the variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & ={x}^{3}+2 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2} \\\\ \\text{d}u & =3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u & ={x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we create a table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=x^3+2.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & -1 & 2 \\\\ u & 1 & 10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n\\int_{-1}^2 \\dfrac{1}{(x^3+2)}\\,x^2\\textrm{d}x=\\int_1^{10} \\dfrac{1}{u}\\,\\cdot \\dfrac{1}{3}\\textrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve it and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{10}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{10}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(u){|}_{1}^{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
